 {"$schema":"fabro-journal-v1","run_id":"01M1MMK5C6B313SY70Y2EPKE82","node":"planner","visit":1,"status":"succeeded","ts":"2026-09-03T22:01:38Z","data":{"painpoints":[],"observations":["fabro-1f5b is a fresh implementation, not verification-only: worktree still has positional opts() plus stepOpts/lastOpts clones in fib_test.go","Spec's default list cross-checked against main.go flag registration — accurate, no contradictions; only nuance is that the new helper must also expose step/last/output which the old opts() signature could not set"]}}
+{"$schema":"fabro-journal-v1","run_id":"01M1MMK5C6B313SY70Y2EPKE82","node":"implementer","visit":1,"status":"succeeded","ts":"2026-09-03T22:06:10Z","data":{"painpoints":[{"text":"The seed-workflow environment has no python3 anywhere on PATH (only mise shims, and `go` itself is unset outside the project dir — `go run` from `/tmp` fails with 'mise ERROR No version is set for shim: go'). Run scripted transforms as `go run /tmp/.../main.go` from the project root, or document a python provider in the run image. Run 01M1MMK5C6B313SY70Y2EPKE82, cost: two failed tool calls rediscovering this."}],"observations":["Composite stepOpts(lastOpts(...)) call sites collapsed naturally into a single newOpts closure starting with `*o = tt.opts` — the fallback kept the transform total rather than needing per-test restructuring of table structs.","TestParseOptionsDefaults now compares parseOptions(nil) against newOpts() defaults instead of a hand-written literal: it still pins parseOptions, but the defaults' single source of truth lives in the helper — a future flag added to options{} must update newOpts or that test catches the drift."]}}
